Z||000002||Xtreme Fiero's||10-26-2000||08:50 AM||||<BR>Ok lets try this, here is a list of import cars.  wichones have you beaten with your fiero and witch oens have beated you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>(easy to fast)<P>1) Civic Type-R<BR>2) Integra GS-R<BR>3) Celica GT-S (new)<BR>4) Integra Type-R<BR>5) RX-7 (3rd gen)<BR>6) 3000GT (non turbo)<BR>7) NSX-T<BR>8) 300ZX Turbo<BR>9) Supra Turbo<P>and of only 2000 model year cars:<P>1 Civic Type-R<BR>2 200SX SE-R<BR>3 Intagra GSR<BR>4 Celica GT-S<BR>5 Integra Type-R<BR>6 Maxima<BR>7 Lexus GS-300/400<BR>8 S2000<BR>9 Skyline GT-R<BR> Do't flame me i didn't get mad and  a do under stand that some of the cars listed are above and beond what a stock fiero can handle. But is't not fair to just say how many imports you killed but how many killed you to?||||reg||3
Z||000003||stimpy||10-26-2000||09:16 AM||||Civic Type R?  Ain't no such beast (in U.S. at least). Could you possibly mean Si?<P>Not too many imports want to mess with me, usually just base models that are easy pckings.  Have been spanked by Acura Integra though.  And played with some kinda Civic w/ an Acura badge on the nose. I could tell he would have walked on me over 85 mph.  But up to 60 like we were messin around with, I had him. hehehe... ||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||10-26-2000||12:39 PM||||where did you find a Skyline on the road? yeah it'll smoke you.. if your up aginst a 240sx and you got smoked theres somthing wrong with your car! but the GT-Rs the N33, and 36 aren't allowed in teh US yet.. a company in Seattle has purchased a few for NHTSA crash testing for them to be taken off the Grey market list.  my $.02    a stock V6 will beat an SI and a S/C Civic EX. and hang with the integras. unless their under forced induction of some kind.. then GOOD LUCK! <BR> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 10-26-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Black88GT||10-26-2000||09:43 PM||||Xtreme, unless you are running a V8 with NOS there is no way you are beating any of those cars except the Civic SI, 200 SX SE-R, Celica GT-S, Integra, Maxima and non turbo 3000 GT.  With ANY stock fiero you could probably only beat a Civic Si, 200 SX SE-R and Maxima (why did you put a sedan in there anyway?)<P><BR>I have raced a Civic Si and a 200 SX SE-R in my GT when it had a very old and beat up 2.8 and I beat them.  However, my friend has a Civic Si with an intake and header, and I drove it.  It feels a little slower then my stock 3.4 with ported manifolds.  Of course it has NO bottom end torque, but once you get that baby revving up to like 8 grand it has good Hp....  <P>So far in my 3.4 I have only 2 of them listed.  First I raced a non turbo Mitsu. 3000 GT and whipped him bad and I raced a supercharged Celica and beat him by a couple car lengths.  Most naturally aspirated foreign cars are easy to beat, like the 300ZX N/A, Supra N/A, MR2 N/A etc. etc. but once they add that forced induction watch out.  I have personally seen a newer Z28 SS get whipped by a Supra TT.  <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 10-27-2000).]||||reg||10
